WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.346
Our 2018 proposal ended with an imidazopyridine drawn

00:00:04.346 --> 00:00:09.216
on paper. The laboratory had yet to close that ring.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.689
We proposed two synthesis routes. Structural

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:22.467
characterization and biological testing would follow if

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.166
the intended molecules were isolated.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:34.411
The planned ring closure did not succeed. We could not

00:00:34.411 --> 00:00:35.996
claim the target heterocycles.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:47.081
What we isolated were three characterized imines, the

00:00:47.081 --> 00:00:50.259
Schiff bases originally meant to serve as

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:50.713
intermediates.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:02.530
We tested their response to anions. One sensor solution

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.703
changed visibly after the addition of cyanide.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.034
Under the reported conditions, its colour shifted from

00:01:17.034 --> 00:01:20.617
yellow to orange. Spectroscopy then tested what that

00:01:20.617 --> 00:01:21.961
visible change meant.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:33.368
The 380-nanometre band declined as the 450-nanometre

00:01:33.368 --> 00:01:38.966
band grew. The detection limit was 1.42 times ten to

00:01:38.966 --> 00:01:41.205
the minus five molar.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.918
Two imines, CMP5 and CMPB, were explored in

00:01:50.918 --> 00:01:54.269
triple-negative breast-cancer cell lines. The assays

00:01:54.269 --> 00:01:57.062
did not establish therapeutic efficacy.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:05.530
Some c-MYC responses contradicted our expectations.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:10.289
Direct PRMT5 engagement was never shown, and

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:12.329
comparisons remained inconclusive.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.270
The final report contained characterized imines and

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.545
unanswered biology. The imidazopyridines we had

00:02:23.545 --> 00:02:26.274
originally drawn were never isolated.
